load @term/seed/type/term
  find term

# A proposition: a statement that is true or false, and in the type-theoretic foundation, a type whose inhabitants are
# its proofs. To prove a proposition is to construct a term of its type, so propositions and types are one. A
# proposition with at most one proof (all proofs equal) is the type-theoretic notion of a truth value. The form carries
# the term language the proposition is a type in.
form proposition
  link statement, like term
